Report window manager edits to the style dialog

The window manager page emits changed() for each of its 22 rows. The dialog
routed that signal to updateChanged(), which raises changed(true) only when
the widgets differ from the Options structure of the preset in use. The page
stores its settings in kwinqtcurverc and owns no field of that structure, so
the host of the dialog never learned of an edit. The Apply button stayed grey
until the user also changed a style option.

The new slot kwinSettingsChanged() raises changed(true) for every report of
the page. The constructor connects the slot after it loads the settings of
the page and of the presets. A load therefore raises no change. The dialog
opens clean.

The page keeps every string, every row and every key of its file.

The change sits on the branch work/wm-kcm of the local tree, as commit 1 of 4.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index ad2193b9..351cc609 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -1257,6 +1257,9 @@ QtCurveConfig::QtCurveConfig(QWidget *parent)
         setupPreview();
         readyForPreview = true;
         updatePreview();
+        // The connect must stay after the loads above. An earlier connect makes
+        // a load of the page report a change.
+        connect(qtcSlot(kwin, changed), qtcSlot(this, kwinSettingsChanged));
     } else {
         stack->setCurrentIndex(kwinPage);
         titleLabel->setVisible(false);
@@ -1755,7 +1758,6 @@ void QtCurveConfig::setupStack()
         kwin->setNote(i18n("<p><b>NOTE:</b><i>The settings here affect the borders drawn around application windows and dialogs - and "
                            "not internal (or MDI) windows. Therefore, these settings will <b>not</b> be reflected in the Preview "
                            "page.</i></p>"));
-        connect(qtcSlot(kwin, changed), qtcSlot(this, updateChanged));
     }
     stack->insertWidget(i, kwin);
     new CStackItem(stackList, i18n("Window Manager"), i++);
@@ -2703,6 +2705,11 @@ void QtCurveConfig::updateEnableStates()
     }
 }
 
+void QtCurveConfig::kwinSettingsChanged()
+{
+    emit changed(true);
+}
